      START
LESSON 1: WHERE YOU ARE

THE SIX SPACES YOU TYPE AFTER ARE THE PROMPT. APL WAITS
THERE. WHAT YOU TYPE IS INDENTED; WHAT APL ANSWERS STARTS
AT THE LEFT MARGIN. TRY:

      2+2
      3×4

IT ANSWERS AT ONCE. THERE IS NO PROGRAM TO WRITE FIRST.
(RETURN TO GO ON, OR STOP) 
A LINE THAT BEGINS WITH A RIGHT PARENTHESIS IS NOT APL BUT
A SYSTEM COMMAND: A WORD TO THE SYSTEM AROUND APL. TWO OF
THEM SAY WHERE YOU ARE. TRY:

      )DIALECT
      )WSID

THE FIRST ANSWERS (A) '70 OR (B) '75. SW-APL HAS TWO MODES,
ONE MODELLED ON THE APL OF 1970 AND ONE ON THE APL OF 1975.
THIS COURSE RUNS IN BOTH; LESSON 16 SAYS HOW THEY DIFFER.
THE SECOND ANSWERS COURSE, THE NAME OF THIS WORKSPACE: THE
FUNCTIONS AND VARIABLES YOU ARE WORKING WITH.
(RETURN TO GO ON, OR STOP) 
WORKSPACES ARE KEPT IN NUMBERED LIBRARIES. TRY:

      )LIBS
      )LIB 2

LIBRARY 0 IS YOURS, WHERE )SAVE WRITES. LIBRARY 1 IS WHAT
SW-APL SHIPS. LIBRARY 2 IS THIS COURSE AND ITS COMPANIONS.
)LIB N LISTS A LIBRARY AND )LOAD N NAME LOADS ONE, WHICH IS
HOW YOU GOT HERE. LESSON 15 IS ABOUT WORKSPACES.
(RETURN TO GO ON, OR STOP) 
WHEN YOU DO NOT KNOW WHAT TO TYPE, ASK. TRY:

      )HELP
      )HELP LIBS

THE FIRST LISTS THE SYSTEM COMMANDS, AND SAYS WHICH ARE
SW-APL'S OWN AND WHICH ARE HISTORICAL. THE SECOND EXPLAINS
ONE. )HELP, )LIBS AND )DIALECT ARE SW-APL'S; THE REST IS
WHAT THE ORIGINAL SYSTEMS HAD.
(RETURN TO GO ON, OR STOP) 
THIS IS HOW A LESSON WORKS: A FEW LINES, SOMETHING TO TRY,
AND A PAUSE. PRESS RETURN TO GO ON, OR TYPE STOP TO LEAVE.
NEXT TAKES YOU TO THE LESSON AFTER THE LAST ONE YOU READ,
CONTENTS LISTS THEM ALL, AND LESSON N GOES TO ANY ONE.

EACH LESSON ENDS WITH A QUIZ. A QUESTION IS ASKED, A PROMPT
OF A QUAD AND A COLON IS PRINTED, AND YOU TYPE THE ANSWER
AS APL: A NUMBER, OR AN EXPRESSION THAT MAKES ONE. STOP
LEAVES A QUIZ TOO.

END OF LESSON 1. TYPE QUIZ 1 TO CHECK, OR NEXT TO GO ON.
      ⍝ The quiz: a right answer, a wrong one, an expression that makes the
      ⍝ right one, and STOP, which leaves without a score.
